  Task 10: Process Creation vs Thread Creation Microbenchmark (N = 1000)
  Student: Rakul K (Reg No: 192525143)
======================================================================

Measuring sequential creation and teardown of 1000 OS Processes...
Measuring concurrent creation and joining of 1000 POSIX Threads...

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Entity               | Total Time (s)   | Avg Cost / Unit  | Speedup     
----------------------------------------------------------------------
1,000 Processes      |         0.8345 s |        834.52 us | 1.00x (Baseline)
1,000 Threads        |         0.0170 s |         16.99 us | 49.12x Faster
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Evaluation:
1. Thread creation is vastly faster because threads share address space and page tables.
2. Process creation requires duplicating task structures, memory maps, and file descriptor tables.
